{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TioC21m7nLvx7tGaiSZCk","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# CRACKMANIA — build plan\n15:## 0. Deliverables, names and ground rules\n40:## 1. The game in one page\n90:## 2. Technology and architecture\n92:### 2.1 Stack (decided)\n114:### 2.2 Getting the engine files\n118:# into the dev folder:\n133:### 2.3 Units, axes and conventions (everyone must use these)\n153:### 2.4 Engine changes (make them first, list them in `engine/CHANGES.md`, mention them in Engine Feedback)\n166:### 2.5 Folder layout and modules\n241:### 2.6 Runtime structure\n272:### 2.7 Build to a single file\n299:## 3. Player experience and controls\n301:### 3.1 The core loop (must feel instant)\n312:### 3.2 Input maps (`game.input` presets; prompts always from `game.input.label(action)` + our glyph sprites)\n340:### 3.3 10-foot UI rules (apply everywhere)\n358:## 4. Core systems\n360:### 4.1 Blocks (the catalogue)\n402:### 4.2 Block paths (centrelines and frames)\n431:### 4.3 Geometry, materials and colliders\n471:### 4.4 The car (validated model — build exactly this, then tune with Dev Mode)\n587:### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\n606:### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\n621:### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\n632:### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\n655:### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\n668:## 5. Modes and features\n670:### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\n702:### 5.2 Race (campaign)\n719:### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\n729:### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\n766:### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\n777:### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\n792:### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\n836:### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\n844:### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\n854:### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \"Dev Mode\")\n873:### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\n888:### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\n904:### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\n916:## 6. Content\n918:### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\n944:### 6.2 Environments\n960:### 6.3 Race tracks (15) — programs validated on the 32×32 grid\n996:### 6.4 Puzzles (6) — fixed blocks and inventories computed from validated solutions\n1014:### 6.5 Survival gauntlets\n1018:### 6.6 Scenery and trackside dressing (`track/deco.js`, seeded by track id)\n1035:### 6.7 Items, rivals and unlockables (what the player collects and fights)\n1046:## 7. Art direction and animation\n1048:### 7.1 The look\n1058:### 7.2 Textures (`env/textures.js`; bake with `E.mkCanvas(w, h)` → `THREE.CanvasTexture`, NearestFilter, repeat)\n1067:### 7.3 Cars (`car/draw.js`, the pen, frame from E1; 25–45 parts each, outlines automatic)\n1082:### 7.4 Characters and props\n1109:### 7.5 Effects (game.particles in 3D, the pen, the camera)\n1118:### 7.6 UI art (pixel sprites via `E.sprite`, `E.font`, `E.ui`)\n1128:### 7.7 Animation list (everything that moves, built on the engine's rigs, tweens and scripts)\n1140:## 8. Audio, story and text\n1142:### 8.1 Music and sound (all synthesized; `game.audio` + `game.audio.ctx`)\n1173:### 8.2 Story beats and characters (`story/story.js`)\n1201:### 8.3 Writing style (TrackMania 2003's)\n1211:### 8.4 Gibberish voices (`audio/babble.js`)\n1224:## 9. Testing\n1226:### 9.1 Headless loader (validated while planning: three r182 and Rapier load and step in Node 24)\n1253:### 9.2 The one command\n1266:### 9.3 Suites and what they check\n1286:### 9.4 Rules for testing\n1292:### 9.5 Browser checks (`tools/browser.mjs`, Playwright 1.63 + Chromium; built HTML opened from `file://`)\n1306:### 9.6 AI Hub harness (`tools/hub.mjs`)\n1318:## 10. Build order and milestones\n1340:## 11. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1359:## 12. Finishing: deliverables, About, exit interview, final reply\n1388:## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n1453:## Appendix B — what was verified during planning (so you can trust it)\nagent.err\nagent.out\ngoal.md\nprompt.md\nunfinished.json\nwork\ngit version 2.56.0\nv24.22.1\n/usr/bin/gh\n/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/python3","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"d242974c-89a6-40ce-adb9-3b8b6a7a81e6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:31.907Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# CRACKMANIA — build plan\n15:## 0. Deliverables, names and ground rules\n40:## 1. The game in one page\n90:## 2. Technology and architecture\n92:### 2.1 Stack (decided)\n114:### 2.2 Getting the engine files\n118:# into the dev folder:\n133:### 2.3 Units, axes and conventions (everyone must use these)\n153:### 2.4 Engine changes (make them first, list them in `engine/CHANGES.md`, mention them in Engine Feedback)\n166:### 2.5 Folder layout and modules\n241:### 2.6 Runtime structure\n272:### 2.7 Build to a single file\n299:## 3. Player experience and controls\n301:### 3.1 The core loop (must feel instant)\n312:### 3.2 Input maps (`game.input` presets; prompts always from `game.input.label(action)` + our glyph sprites)\n340:### 3.3 10-foot UI rules (apply everywhere)\n358:## 4. Core systems\n360:### 4.1 Blocks (the catalogue)\n402:### 4.2 Block paths (centrelines and frames)\n431:### 4.3 Geometry, materials and colliders\n471:### 4.4 The car (validated model — build exactly this, then tune with Dev Mode)\n587:### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\n606:### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\n621:### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\n632:### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\n655:### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\n668:## 5. Modes and features\n670:### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\n702:### 5.2 Race (campaign)\n719:### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\n729:### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\n766:### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\n777:### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\n792:### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\n836:### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\n844:### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\n854:### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \"Dev Mode\")\n873:### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\n888:### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\n904:### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\n916:## 6. Content\n918:### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\n944:### 6.2 Environments\n960:### 6.3 Race tracks (15) — programs validated on the 32×32 grid\n996:### 6.4 Puzzles (6) — fixed blocks and inventories computed from validated solutions\n1014:### 6.5 Survival gauntlets\n1018:### 6.6 Scenery and trackside dressing (`track/deco.js`, seeded by track id)\n1035:### 6.7 Items, rivals and unlockables (what the player collects and fights)\n1046:## 7. Art direction and animation\n1048:### 7.1 The look\n1058:### 7.2 Textures (`env/textures.js`; bake with `E.mkCanvas(w, h)` → `THREE.CanvasTexture`, NearestFilter, repeat)\n1067:### 7.3 Cars (`car/draw.js`, the pen, frame from E1; 25–45 parts each, outlines automatic)\n1082:### 7.4 Characters and props\n1109:### 7.5 Effects (game.particles in 3D, the pen, the camera)\n1118:### 7.6 UI art (pixel sprites via `E.sprite`, `E.font`, `E.ui`)\n1128:### 7.7 Animation list (everything that moves, built on the engine's rigs, tweens and scripts)\n1140:## 8. Audio, story and text\n1142:### 8.1 Music and sound (all synthesized; `game.audio` + `game.audio.ctx`)\n1173:### 8.2 Story beats and characters (`story/story.js`)\n1201:### 8.3 Writing style (TrackMania 2003's)\n1211:### 8.4 Gibberish voices (`audio/babble.js`)\n1224:## 9. Testing\n1226:### 9.1 Headless loader (validated while planning: three r182 and Rapier load and step in Node 24)\n1253:### 9.2 The one command\n1266:### 9.3 Suites and what they check\n1286:### 9.4 Rules for testing\n1292:### 9.5 Browser checks (`tools/browser.mjs`, Playwright 1.63 + Chromium; built HTML opened from `file://`)\n1306:### 9.6 AI Hub harness (`tools/hub.mjs`)\n1318:## 10. Build order and milestones\n1340:## 11. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1359:## 12. Finishing: deliverables, About, exit interview, final reply\n1388:## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n1453:## Appendix B — what was verified during planning (so you can trust it)\nagent.err\nagent.out\ngoal.md\nprompt.md\nunfinished.json\nwork\ngit version 2.56.0\nv24.22.1\n/usr/bin/gh\n/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/python3","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016TioC21m7nLvx7tGaiSZCk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
