{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtWeJQ3wkR8grsgyJGVXJ6","type":"tool_result","content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<!--\n  my-3D2dge (My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine), 3D racing kit v0.85.2 (dev-build)\n  https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n\n  AI MODELS: this one file is the engine, the 3D engine, their documentation and one 3D game to copy.\n    1. Read the 3D engine's manual: the comment at the top of the script marked \"inlined from engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js\".\n       Then the API card in <script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\"> below, for what the 2D engine still does in\n       a 3D game: the game and its scenes, input, the rigs and their moves, the HUD (font, ui, menus), sound.\n    2. The engines are the scripts marked \"inlined from engine/...\". They are yours to change: fix, extend or rewrite\n       any of them as you see fit (their sources, readable, are in the repository's engine/).\n       Its modules follow it, each a script marked \"inlined from engine/modules/<name>.js\" that starts with its\n       manual: drive.\n       It leaves out what its game never calls (the kit diet): 1b MORE EASINGS; 2b SPRITE FRAMES, TURNS AND SWAPS;\n       10d TWEENS AND SCRIPTS; 10f TRANSITIONS; 10g WEATHER; 10h INPUT SEQUENCES; 10k SAVE SLOTS; 13 TILE MAP; 14\n       FLOW FIELD; 16 PLATFORM MAP; 16b PLATFORMER; 16c TRAVERSAL; 17b ACTIONS; 17c MOVER; 17d PERCEPTION; 18\n       BULLETS; 19 SPATIAL HASH; 21g SOLID SHAPES; 22 GPU LIGHTING (WebGPU). Calling one of them warns, naming its\n       section (a class throws). dist/my-3d2dge-3d.html has both engines whole.\n    3. The game\n- If you can run commands: `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html` (your page; add `#scene` to jump to a scene). It presses start, plays, cycles the views, prints how much of the screen is filled and how many colors it uses, adds look notes (flat areas, checkerboard dithering, low contrast, a thin pa\n- Animation variety: every character has its own moves from `E.MOVES` (not one shared swing), enemies telegraph with a visible wind-up, and reactions play out (hurt, knockback, `down`, victory `cheer`).\n\n</script>\n<script type=\"importmap\">\n{\n  \"imports\": {\n    \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n    \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n    \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\"\n  }\n}\n</script>\n<style>\nhtml,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}\n8:       Then the API card in <script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\"> below, for what the 2D engine still does in\n36:<script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\">\n247:- **Modules** (`engine/modules/<name>.js`; `modules/` in the handoff package): general systems in files of their own, each a `<script>` after the engine, its header its manual (read it there, or i\n262:<script type=\"importmap\">\n302:<script>\n320:<script>\n398:<script>\n440:<script type=\"module\">\n457:<script type=\"importmap\">{ \"imports\": { \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n463:<script src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge.js\"><\\/script>                   the 2D engine, a classic script, first\n464:<script type=\"module\" src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"><\\/script>  this file\n465:<script type=\"module\" src=\"game.js\"><\\/script>                your game, a module (const E = My3D2dge;)\n704:<script type=\"module\">\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050314__x1f94fb/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"d34b22a1-e6f9-425d-adf7-24785cac7350","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:05:59.566Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<!--\n  my-3D2dge (My \"3D\