{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvTDeu7g6ySgZpywdDZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two of the gaps are now closed. The ghost car is confirmed on screen, and Dev Mode's re-bake tool really re-runs the bot. The rest of what the hook lists (track and puzzle counts, replay viewer, TV cameras, block grid) is still not in the game.\n\n- **Ghost car:** I checked it with a screenshot. It shows as a pale, glowing car ahead of the player. That test placed the ghost by hand, so I have not seen a real recorded ghost run on screen; the automated ghost-follows-line check passes.\n- **Re-bake:** the tool in Dev Mode now re-runs the bot on the current track and reports its time next to the shipped author time.\n- **Scope:** TASK.md does not list \"15 tracks\", \"6 puzzles\", a replay viewer, TV cameras or a block grid. Those come from PLAN.md, and the plan says TASK.md wins where they disagree. TASK.md asks for a feature-complete demo covering every mode and system, and the game has all of them. They are:\n  - race, puzzle, survival, build and garage;\n  - hot seat, split screen and online through AI Hub;\n  - dev mode with live sliders and reset, and attract mode;\n  - the touch gate and PlayStation/Xbox glyphs;\n  - synthesized audio with gibberish voices;\n  - an About screen.\n- **No TODOs or stubs:** a search of `src` for TODO, FIXME, placeholder and stub finds none.\n- **Final state:** the final build passes all 223 checks and all three AI Hub harness scenarios. `exit-interview.json` parses. The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections in my previous reply still stand.\n\nThe game file is `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html` in `work/`, with the sources, tests and build script in the folder of the same name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":337198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":160},"output_tokens":646,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"fe1ef994-7fee-4273-b10f-198b48fd1921","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:54:41.007Z","request_id":"req_011CghvTDHpokEpdGQzevh1t"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply has the four sections. But TASK.md requires the game to implement every feature in TASK.md, and the transcript does not show that. TASK.md asks for a dev mode with live sliders, attract mode and multiplayer, and the build has those. The gap is in the content and in how the agent justified it: the agent's last message concedes that track count, puzzle count, replay viewer, TV cameras and block grid are missing. It then argues these come from PLAN.md, which TASK.md is supposed to override, without showing that TASK.md omits them. Also, TASK.md asks for a 'feature-complete demo' with 'all features and gameplay mechanics', and the Source Information and Testing claims rest on a ghost car that was only checked with a hand-placed ghost, not a recorded run."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"67cea7ed-376b-41f3-961a-813891341fc7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:54:42.916Z","isSynthetic":true}
