{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvmrBbv5R3zzg2q4PpL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The earlier replies overstated what I'd shown, so here is what is now checked and what is still missing.\n\n**Recorded ghost.** There is now a test for it, and it passes. The autopilot drives D2 and its run is recorded. On the next run the ghost car spawns from that recording. Over 10 or more seconds of racing it stays within 40 units of the player car, which drives the same line. The full suite passes: 225 checks, 0 failed.\n\n**Scope against TASK.md.** I searched TASK.md for \"replay\", \"TV cam\", \"block grid\", \"15 tracks\" and \"puzzle\". Replays appear only inside the attract-mode sentence (\"looping AI-played demo or scripted replay\"), which the AI demo satisfies. TASK.md names no track count, no puzzle count, no replay viewer, no TV cameras and no block grid. Those numbers come only from PLAN.md. TASK.md asks for a feature-complete vertical slice that shows every mechanic: Dev Mode with sliders and reset, attract mode, multiplayer (hot seat, split screen, AI Hub online), 10-foot controller-first UI, glyphs, touch gate, synthesized audio and voices, narrative, About screen, and the exit interview.\n\n**What is in the game.**\n- Race: 9 tracks across 3 lands, with medals, coppers, unlocks and a ghost of your best run.\n- Puzzle and Build: 3 puzzles; Build is a block-chain editor with costs, undo, 6 save slots and share codes.\n- Survival: 3 gauntlets of 3 rounds against 3 ghost rivals.\n- Hot seat and split screen, online through AI Hub, garage, Dev Mode, attract mode, touch gate and an About screen.\n- The Source Information and feedback sections are in the About screen.\n\n**Still missing, as I said before.** The plan's loop-the-loop and block-grid editor, a replay viewer and TV cameras are not implemented. I judged them out of scope because TASK.md doesn't ask for them. If you want them anyway, say so and I'll scope it.\n\nThe game is still `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html` in `work/`, and `exit-interview.json` still parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:03:14\n- **Source:** TrackMania (2003, Nadeo)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade racing (time attack) with a track-building puzzle mode; third-person chase camera (far, close, bumper), top-down map in the editor\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 2D engine v0.85.2 plus its 3D engine on three.js r182 (WebGPU, WebGL 2 fallback) and Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12 to one inlined HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's low-resolution toon-shaded 3D with ink outlines; cars, gates, boost pads, ghosts and cacti drawn by code; pixel-font UI; three lands (Dustbowl, Hedgerow, Frostpeak)\n- **Animation:** The engine's vehicle tilt and steering animation, tweens, particles and the pen; gates, pads, ghost hulls and the finish orbit camera animated by code\n- **Audio:** All synthesized with Web Audio: songs per land, effects, an engine hum and tyre hiss, Animalese-style gibberish voices for Coco and Gus; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode: everyone time-attacks the same track for three minutes, with own card, ghost cars of other players, progress and one result\n- **Testing:** 225 headless checks behind one command (`node tools/test.mjs`), the AI Hub harness in Chromium (3 scenarios), and a few screenshots under SwiftShader\n- **Research:** Plan research on TrackMania (2003); engine manual, API card and AI Hub protocol read\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in Chromium via Playwright)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 10 real defects:\n  - The countdown reversed the car.\n  - A story dialog froze the race after a deep link.\n  - A course with negative coordinates fell outside the level.\n  - Scenery stood on the road.\n  - Survival results never appeared.\n  - Split-screen players were left behind after quitting.\n  - The online card used an unknown input action.\n  - The attract demo exited on a mouse artifact.\n  - Baked medal times went stale after a clock fix.\n  - The ghost car was drawn opaque and hidden inside the player's car.\n- **Critical or game-breaking:** Four: the reversing countdown, the frozen race, the course outside the level, and the tree on the road.\n- **Most helpful test:** Bots drive every track and puzzle solution with zero respawns, plus the scripted playthrough of all nine races through the real menus.\n- **Least helpful test:** The SwiftShader screenshots (slow, and they can't show physics or timing) and the AI Hub harness, which passed first time and found nothing.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `world.track` and `world.vehicle` gave a banked road, walls, boost pads, E.Car handling and Rapier jumps over pits, plus `game.advance` determinism, the pause shell with settings and glyphs, and the pen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes.\n  - Level tiles start at world 0, so negative coordinates fell off the level.\n  - Synthetic input taps mark the device as touch.\n  - A held brake at standstill drives the vehicle backwards.\n  - Vehicles ignore `fade`, so ghosts can't be translucent.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The course compiler, the run clock and gates, the pure-pursuit bot, the segment editor and puzzles, the 10-foot UI kit, survival rivals, and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **Hardest part:** Getting loops, block grids and surface-following cars out of an engine whose vehicle is a rolling ball on a mesh, and bundling the 3D engine, three and Rapier into one file.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** Only the input glyph default (now PlayStation) and the glyph setting (PlayStation or Xbox), as TASK.md asks.\n- **One change I'd make:** Let `world.track` build several sections with real gaps and loops, make vehicles honour `fade`, and give input an analog accessor for triggers.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The concrete plan, with units, validated numbers, a test list and the AI Hub flow written out.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's scope (15 tracks, 6 puzzles, a block grid with loops, a custom Rapier car) is too big for a medium-effort session, and its file name differs from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** Choosing what to cut from the plan while keeping every TASK.md feature.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark which plan parts are essential and which are stretch, give a smaller tier for lower efforts, and use one file name in both documents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":339754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":637},"output_tokens":761,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"95fb8bb5-7040-4657-afb7-8a626e83db45","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:59:03.311Z","request_id":"req_011CghvmqmHr89JcoKxnkxpa"}
