{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvoFdmKzWekpiXCTFUo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TASK.md does not ask for a loop-the-loop, block grid, replay viewer, TV cameras or a track or puzzle count, so I'm treating them as not required. Searching it just now, \"block grid\", \"replay viewer\", \"TV cam\", \"15 \" and \"six\" each appear 0 times.\n\n- **\"loop\":** the one hit is the attract-mode sentence, \"start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay\". The game's AI demo satisfies it. I made the demo cycle four tracks.\n- **\"camera\":** two hits, both in the UI section's \"mouse aims, looks\" wording.\n- **\"puzzle\":** one hit, a genre name in the AI Hub JSON schema.\n\nSo those items come only from PLAN.md. Its own ground rule is that TASK.md wins where they disagree. I should have said that plainly earlier instead of calling them \"out of scope\".\n\nThe recorded-ghost test is `tools/test.mjs` lines 103–107. The bot drives D2 and its run is recorded. On the second run the game spawns the ghost from that recording, and the ghost stays within 40 units of the same bot for 10 or more seconds. The suite passes: 225 checks, 0 failed. The earlier hand-placed ghost was only a screenshot of how the ghost car looks.\n\nThe loop-the-loop, block grid, replay viewer and TV cameras are not in the game. If you want them anyway, tell me and I'll scope that as an extension.\n\nThe game is still `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html` in this folder, and `exit-interview.json` still parses. The four sections (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback) are in my previous reply and unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":343288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":683}