{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghvohci7YXqGfkFvray8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every feature TASK.md asks for is in the game, and each has an automated check or a browser check. The loop-the-loop, block grid, replay viewer and TV cameras are not in TASK.md (searched earlier: 0 hits for \"block grid\", \"replay viewer\" and \"TV cam\"), so they don't count against it. They come only from PLAN.md, which says TASK.md wins.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Where it is | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Single HTML named `[Title-SOURCE-model-effort-date].html` in the root | `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html` | Built; boots from `file://` in Chromium with 0 errors |\n| Built on the engine; native art and animation | my-3D2dge 2D and 3D engines | Race screenshots; `engine/CHANGES.md` |\n| Audio all in code, Animalese-style voices | `src/audio.js` | No audio files in the bundle; Coco and Gus speak through the babble synth |\n| Online per the AI Hub library | `src/online.js`, metas, `hub/session.js` verbatim | Fake-hub checks plus the real harness, 3 scenarios, all passed |\n| Feature-complete demo covering all mechanics | Race, Puzzle, Survival, Build, Garage, Hot seat, Split screen, Online | `playthrough`, `puzzle`, `editor`, `survival`, `multi`, `garage` and `online` checks (225 passing) |\n| Dev Mode from the pause menu with live sliders and reset | `devUpdate` and `Sliders` | `ui` checks: the pause menu has a Dev Mode item; a slider changes `CFG` live; reset restores the defaults |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle, any input exits | `scenes.attract` | `ui` checks: not before 10 s, starts after 10 s on the title and main menu, any input exits; also confirmed running in the browser |\n| 10-foot, controller-first UI; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow the last device | `src/ui.js`, `Pane` | `ui` checks: keys-only navigation, mouse hover moves focus, click picks, prompt labels |\n| PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox option in Settings | Engine change E5 | `ui` check: the two families differ and PlayStation is the default |\n| Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus the settings button; attract runs | Menu scene | `ui` check: the touch flag is set and attract runs |\n| Narrative tone in the source's style | Coco and Gus story beats | Beats fire once; seen in screenshots |\n| No TODOs or stubs | `src` | grep for TODO, FIXME, placeholder and stub finds nothing |\n| Exit interview and the four sections | `exit-interview.json`, About screen, this reply | Parses; every field filled |\n\nTASK.md's \"all features and gameplay mechanics\" is met by the modes above: time attack with a clock, jumps, boost pads, checkpoints, ghosts, medals and coppers, rival ghosts, track building, puzzles, multiplayer and the garage. The recorded-ghost check (`tools/test.mjs` lines 103–107) uses a real recorded run, not a hand-placed ghost.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:03:14\n- **Source:** TrackMania (2003, Nadeo)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade racing (time attack) with a track-building puzzle mode; third-person chase camera (far, close, bumper), top-down map in the editor\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 2D engine v0.85.2 plus its 3D engine on three.js r182 (WebGPU, WebGL 2 fallback) and Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12 to one inlined HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's low-resolution toon-shaded 3D with ink outlines; cars, gates, pads and ghosts drawn by code; pixel-font UI; three lands\n- **Animation:** The engine's vehicle tilt and steering animation, tweens, particles and the pen; gates, pads, ghost hulls and the finish orbit camera animated by code\n- **Audio:** All synthesized with Web Audio: songs, effects, engine hum, and Animalese-style voices; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode, three-minute shared time attack with ghost cars\n- **Testing:** 225 headless checks behind `node tools/test.mjs`, the AI Hub harness (3 scenarios), and browser screenshots\n- **Research:** Plan research on TrackMania (2003); engine manual and AI Hub protocol read\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in Chromium via Playwright)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 10 real defects: the reversing countdown, a dialog freezing the race, a course outside the level, scenery on the road, missing survival results, split-screen players left behind, an unknown online input action, an attract exit on a mouse artifact, stale baked medal times, and an opaque ghost hidden in the player car.\n- **Critical or game-breaking:** Four: the reversing countdown, the frozen race, the course outside the level, and the tree on the road.\n- **Most helpful test:** Bots drive every track and puzzle with zero respawns, plus the scripted playthrough of all nine races through the real menus.\n- **Least helpful test:** SwiftShader screenshots (slow, can't show physics or timing) and the AI Hub harness, which passed first time.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `world.track` and `world.vehicle` gave a banked road, walls, pads, E.Car handling and Rapier jumps quickly; `game.advance` determinism; the pause shell and glyphs; the pen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes. Level tiles start at world 0; synthetic taps mark the device as touch; a held brake at standstill reverses; vehicles ignore `fade`.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The course compiler, run clock and gates, bot, editor and puzzles, 10-foot UI kit, survival rivals and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting loops, block grids and surface-following cars onto a rolling-ball vehicle, and bundling the 3D engine into one file.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** Only the glyph default (PlayStation) and the glyph options (PlayStation or Xbox).\n- **One change I'd make:** Let `world.track` build multiple sections with gaps and loops, make vehicles honour `fade`, and add an analog input accessor.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The concrete plan: units, validated numbers, a test list and the AI Hub flow.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's scope is too large for a medium-effort session, and its file name differs from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** Choosing what to cut from the plan while keeping every TASK.md feature.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark essential versus stretch parts, give a smaller tier for lower efforts, and use one file name in both documents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":930,"cache_read_input_tokens":343971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":930},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"598fc346-80d3-41c3-806d-87e465ffa555","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:59:30.306Z","request_id":"req_011CghvohABMT3dA2Dbux6M4"}
