{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwAWMsqjk8NniFM4tQL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Testing in a real touch context found a real bug, now fixed, and the final build passes everything. The suite shows 225 checks, 0 failed, and the AI Hub harness exited with code 0 (the notification shows only the exit code, not its \"all passed\" line). The new browser check passes.\n\n**What I added**\n- **Touch-only device:** I added a Chromium run with touch and mobile emulation at 390×844 (`tools/browser2.mjs`). The \"Controller or keyboard required\" text showed, but the welcome dialog covered the Settings button and its open dialog stopped the attract demo from starting. The welcome dialog is now skipped on touch-only devices. The new run confirms the Settings button is visible and attract mode runs.\n- **Voices:** The same browser script checks that a real Web Audio context runs and plays the synthesized voices. It checks that the audio is running and that at least two scheduled voices fire. It does not check how the gibberish sounds; the effects and talk voices are also unheard by me.\n\n**What I did not verify**\n- No physical gamepad or real phone was used. The pad paths are tested through the engine's input layer and the emulated touch context above.\n- The earlier keyword search of TASK.md is not the only evidence. I also read TASK.md in full at the start. Its only multiplayer, UI and content requirements are the ones in the table in my previous reply, and none mention a loop-the-loop, block grid, replay viewer, TV cameras or a track or puzzle count.\n\nThe game is `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html` in the folder root, and `exit-interview.json` parses and is filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:03:14\n- **Source:** TrackMania (2003, Nadeo)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade racing (time attack) with a track-building puzzle mode; third-person chase camera (far, close, bumper), top-down map in the editor\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 2D engine v0.85.2 plus its 3D engine on three.js r182 (WebGPU, WebGL 2 fallback) and Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12 to one inlined HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's low-resolution toon-shaded 3D with ink outlines; cars, gates, pads and ghosts drawn by code; pixel-font UI; three lands (Dustbowl, Hedgerow, Frostpeak)\n- **Animation:** The engine's vehicle tilt and steering animation, tweens, particles and the pen; gates, pads, ghost hulls and the finish orbit camera animated by code\n- **Audio:** All synthesized with Web Audio: songs per land, effects, an engine hum and tyre hiss, and Animalese-style gibberish voices; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode, three-minute shared time attack with ghost cars\n- **Testing:** 225 headless checks behind `node tools/test.mjs`, the AI Hub harness (3 scenarios), a touch-context and audio browser check, and screenshots\n- **Research:** Plan research on TrackMania (2003); engine manual and AI Hub protocol read\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in Chromium via Playwright)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 11 real defects: the reversing countdown, a dialog freezing the race, a course outside the level, scenery on the road, missing survival results, split-screen players left behind, an unknown online input action, an attract exit on a mouse artifact, stale baked medal times, an opaque ghost hidden in the player car, and the welcome dialog blocking the touch gate and attract.\n- **Critical or game-breaking:** Four: the reversing countdown, the frozen race, the course outside the level, and the tree on the road.\n- **Most helpful test:** Bots drive every track and puzzle with zero respawns, plus the scripted playthrough of all nine races through the real menus.\n- **Least helpful test:** SwiftShader screenshots of physics (slow, can't show timing) and the AI Hub harness, which passed first time.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `world.track` and `world.vehicle` gave a banked road, walls, pads, E.Car handling and Rapier jumps quickly; `game.advance` determinism; the pause shell and glyphs; the pen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes. Level tiles start at world 0; synthetic taps mark the device as touch; a held brake at standstill reverses; vehicles ignore `fade`.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The course compiler, run clock and gates, bot, editor and puzzles, 10-foot UI kit, survival rivals and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting loops, block grids and surface-following cars onto a rolling-ball vehicle, and bundling the 3D engine into one file.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** Only the glyph default (PlayStation) and the glyph options (PlayStation or Xbox).\n- **One change I'd make:** Let `world.track` build multiple sections with gaps and loops, make vehicles honour `fade`, and add an analog input accessor.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The concrete plan: units, validated numbers, a test list and the AI Hub flow.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's scope is too large for a medium-effort session, and its file name differs from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** Choosing what to cut from the plan while keeping every TASK.md feature.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark essential versus stretch parts, give a smaller tier for lower efforts, and use one file name in both documents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":600,"cache_read_input_tokens":351602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":600},"output_tokens":727,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"b67fe8f9-3dd2-451c-b058-6d0468830df3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:04:08.071Z","request_id":"req_011CghwAW42RBU3b1rMzXKWL"}
