{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4TPWL7GuqX9WRqQRrux5T","type":"tool_result","content":"SOURCE: TrackMania 2003\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html]. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included \n\n...\n36:Scope\n37-\n38-Create a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n39-\n40:Include a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"3640d2d6-d89a-4269-9afc-08e6ee5e5f93","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:04:12.003Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"SOURCE: TrackMania 2003\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best