{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwD6taT9c2WaEQnubK6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The deliverables are complete. Four items are not feature gaps, and I can't verify them further in this environment:\n\n- **Audio quality:** I can't hear the audio.\n- **Controller and phone:** I had no physical gamepad or phone; pads and touch are covered through the engine's input layer and an emulated touch context.\n- **Visual quality:** screenshots are all I can inspect, and I checked them.\n- **Scope:** I read TASK.md in full at the start and again quoted its Scope section; it asks for a feature-complete vertical slice and names no loops, block grid, replay viewer, TV cameras or track and puzzle counts. Those come only from PLAN.md, which defers to TASK.md.\n\nVerified state: `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050314.html` is in the folder root. `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled. The suite shows 225 checks, 0 failed. The AI Hub harness passes and Chromium runs with no errors.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:03:14\n- **Source:** TrackMania (2003, Nadeo)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade racing (time attack) with a track-building puzzle mode; third-person chase camera (far, close, bumper), top-down map in the editor\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 2D engine v0.85.2 plus its 3D engine on three.js r182 (WebGPU, WebGL 2 fallback) and Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12 to one inlined HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's low-resolution toon-shaded 3D with ink outlines; cars, gates, pads and ghosts drawn by code; pixel-font UI; three lands (Dustbowl, Hedgerow, Frostpeak)\n- **Animation:** The engine's vehicle tilt and steering animation, tweens, particles and the pen; gates, pads, ghost hulls and the finish orbit camera animated by code\n- **Audio:** All synthesized with Web Audio: songs per land, effects, engine hum and tyre hiss, Animalese-style gibberish voices; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode, three-minute shared time attack with ghost cars\n- **Testing:** 225 headless checks behind `node tools/test.mjs`, the AI Hub harness (3 scenarios), a touch-context and audio browser check, and screenshots\n- **Research:** Plan research on TrackMania (2003); engine manual and AI Hub protocol read\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in Chromium via Playwright)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 11 real defects: the reversing countdown, a dialog freezing the race, a course outside the level, scenery on the road, missing survival results, split-screen players left behind, an unknown online input action, an attract exit on a mouse artifact, stale baked medal times, an opaque ghost, and the welcome dialog blocking the touch gate.\n- **Critical or game-breaking:** Four: the reversing countdown, the frozen race, the course outside the level, and the tree on the road.\n- **Most helpful test:** Bots drive every track and puzzle with zero respawns, plus the scripted playthrough through the real menus.\n- **Least helpful test:** SwiftShader screenshots of physics, and the AI Hub harness, which passed first time.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `world.track` and `world.vehicle` gave a banked road, pads and Rapier jumps quickly; `game.advance` determinism; the pause shell and glyphs; the pen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes. Level tiles start at world 0; synthetic taps mark the device as touch; a held brake at standstill reverses; vehicles ignore `fade`.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The course compiler, run clock and gates, bot, editor and puzzles, 10-foot UI kit, survival rivals and the AI Hub ghost layer.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting loops, block grids and surface-following cars onto a rolling-ball vehicle, and bundling the 3D engine into one file.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** Only the glyph default (PlayStation) and glyph options (PlayStation or Xbox).\n- **One change I'd make:** Let `world.track` build multiple sections with gaps and loops, make vehicles honour `fade`, and add an analog input accessor.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The concrete plan: units, validated numbers, a test list and the AI Hub flow.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's scope is too large for a medium-effort session, and its file name differs from TASK.md's.\n- **Hardest thing:** Choosing what to cut from the plan while keeping every TASK.md feature.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark essential versus stretch parts, give a smaller tier for lower efforts, and use one file name in both documents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":358008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"133e450b-8b13-41c9-9125-2ea73f490cb8","uuid":"a2648b21-75d3-45c4-b7cb-97acffe1ce0a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:04:41.462Z","request_id":"req_011CghwD6UXgW5mLAhmeSmvb"}
